text:
The moon was bright an' clear,

And I took her hand and kissed it sweet;

But I couldn't find my love to greet!

For example,

Take this world with its pleasures and pain;

The joys it brings are sweet indeed, but there's no place like home, my dear friend!

I'll be up before daylight to milk the cow;

Then off we go down on the farm-yard floor ;

While mother she will say, " Johny, Johny."

The rose is lovely, but not for me;
 No scent, no sweetness; and what beauty

 Can stand beside this other flower?

 The purple is strong, yet gentle too;

I never can be tired, my God to me is the ocean,

The azure sea that shines with light and freedom;
And all around it are ships laden with dreams!
